# Fantasy / Tools / Projections UI

Read `docs/PRODUCT.md` first. User-facing name is **Fantasy**, not Draft Hub.
Layout craft (spacing, alignment, tables, selects): `.cursor/rules/frontend-craft.mdc`.
Page-specific do-nots: the matching row in `frontend/src/livingSurfaces.js`.

## Layout

- Resolve the screen in `frontend/src/livingSurfaces.js` and open that `page` / `copy` before changing chrome.
- Pages: `HubPage` with `hub-experience-page` when the surface is a decision page.
- Hero + sticky summary: `HubExperienceHero`, `HubExperienceLayout`, `HubExperienceSummary` in `HubUILayout.jsx`.
- Sections: `HubSection`, `HubTableCard`, `HubToolbar`, `HubAlert` / `HubAlertStack`.
- Intro copy: `HubTabIntro` only when the page is not already using the experience hero.
- Live draft (`DraftRoom` while a draft is running): keep the board-first layout. Do not add the two-column settings chrome. Auction theater lives on the nominee card (bid pulse, draining clock, 1s SOLD hold). Do not toast a sold result in the header.
- Do not create a second hero, chip, or summary component. Extend the existing ones.
- Idle Draft, Mock, and the live room share `DraftSeat`. Do not fork YOU / Open · Take tiles.

## Copy and data

- User-visible strings belong in `*Presentation.js` (`rulesPresentation.js`, `leagueHomePresentation.js`, `gameCenterPresentation.js`, `dfsToolPresentation.js`, `bestBallPresentation.js`, `insightsPresentation.js`, `leagueAccessCopy.js`, `vibeRankingsPresentation.js`, `strategyRankPresentation.js`, `capPlannerPresentation.js`, `officeContractsPresentation.js`, `rosterPresentation.js`, `projectionsPresentation.js`). Home and Game center share `interpretStandings`. Do not invent a 1–10 seed from 0–0.
- Page copy states the decision and the cost of getting it wrong. No slogan that could sit on another app.
- Rules preview, validation, and summary: `mergeLeagueRules`, `validateLeagueSettings`, `contractSchedule`, `rulesSummary`.
- Free-agent button/banner copy: `acquisitionWindow.js`.
- Home next-action voice: `leagueHomePresentation.js`.

## Chat

Chat chrome lives on `FantasyChatDock.jsx` (header comment) and `docs/PRODUCT.md`. Use the dock on shared Fantasy pages when a real league is selected. Hide for solo / unconnected contexts and in a live draft room that already has integrated chat.

## League behavior

- Rules are readable by members (`Commissioner managed`). Roster management is commissioner/co-commissioner only.
- Old `/hub/office` and commissioner routes must keep working; redirect, do not break bookmarks.
- Players-tab adds follow the calendar. Offseason trades: surviving contracts only.
- Suggested bid, wherever it renders (Strategy, Free agents, live room), shows the league scoring name and the Rules risk posture beside the number.
- Freshness is one shared `ensureLeagueFreshness` call. Do not add a second `/freshness` fetch on a destination.
- Cache `/api/hub/home` like other destinations so a tab switch is not a 6s refetch.
- Do not fetch Projections APIs (`/api/injuries`, `meta/*`, `ros/*`, `predict/*`, `draft/*`) on Fantasy pages that do not render them.
- Headshots must match roster photos (`HubMediaImg` / existing media helpers). Request the painted size (`?w=48|96|256` for hub media; ESPN combiner / Sleeper thumb for remotes). Do not fetch the studio original for a 22px mark.
- `GET /api/hub/value-sheet` is one in-flight request per season/rules key. Cap-sheet updates must not abort and refetch it.
- Chat polls back off when the tab is hidden. Do not keep a 12s `chat/league/messages` loop on a background tab.
- Strategy face-off pairs the same position only. Do not pair RB vs WR as a FLEX toss-up.

## Visual / a11y

- Tokens from `tokens.css`, `product-hierarchy.css`, `product-rhythm.css`, and `fantasy-phone.css`. No one-off neon, no new accent color.
- Laptop: summary rail may drop under the hero. No horizontal page scroll at 1024 / 1280 / 1440.
- Long Tools / pool tables window against page scroll. Do not nest a `.table-wrap` scroller.
- Primary save/action stays visible. Disabled controls explain why.
- Exclusive choice groups use `role="radiogroup"` / `role="radio"`. Destination subnavs set `aria-selected`.
- After a build or validity verdict, announce with `aria-live` and move focus or scroll the result into view.
- `details > summary` stays `list-item` so the disclosure triangle shows.
- Dense pool tables let the page own vertical scroll and stick the header. Lock/Skip accessible names include the player.
- Numbered step sequences include every visible step or drop the numerals.
- Do not keep hidden Fantasy panes in the DOM of another destination. Unmount keep-alives when the tab is not showing.
- Rank bars share a fixed track and a field scale. Never let the value label steal track width. Do not paint every bar teal/green.
- Trades Send / Get / Cut expose `aria-pressed` and an accessible name that includes the player and destination.
- League-strip menus (Switch league, Sync league) must paint above the Fantasy page below the strip, not only above Needs attention. `.draft-hub > *` is pinned at z-index 1 so atmosphere stays under content — raise `.hub-league-context-bar` to `--z-dropdown` or portal the menu.
